infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two kinds of state with opposite physics
  desc Server state is a cache of another's truth; client state is UI truth you own
  compares
    - label Server state
      children
        - label Owner: the server
          desc Your copy is a cache of someone else's data
        - label Asynchronous, stale on arrival
          desc Fetched over the network; old the moment it lands
        - label Shared, mutated by others
          desc Concurrent writers drift every private copy
        - label Has a cache lifecycle
          desc Dedupe, revalidate, invalidate on mutation, GC
        - label Lives in the query cache
          desc Keyed entries; mutations invalidate the keys
    - label Client state
      children
        - label Owner: you (the UI)
          desc The UI is the source of truth
        - label Synchronous, always correct
          desc Set in place; no fetch, no staleness
        - label Private to this session
          desc Dies on unmount or reload
        - label No cache lifecycle
          desc Nothing remote to revalidate against
        - label Lives in useState / reducer / store
          desc The client tools from lessons 1-3
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
